        <body>
            <div xml:id="d303">

                <pb facs="0706" n="664" xml:id="pg664"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 303</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The Foreign Ministers of the United States, the United Kingdom, and France met in
                    Washington on September 10–14 for a series of conferences covering a wide range
                    of subjects including revision of the Treaty of Peace with Italy. These
                    tripartite meetings were preceded by 2 days of bilateral discussions between the
                    Foreign Ministers. Revision of the Italian Peace Treaty was discussed by
                        Acheson and Schuman during their meeting on September 11 and
                    by the three Foreign Ministers during their fifth meeting on September 13. For
                    the minutes of these meetings, see <ref target="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg_1249"
                        >volume III, Part 1, pages 1249</ref> and <ref
                        target="frus:frus1951v03p1/pg_1279">1279</ref>.</p>
                <p>In preparation for these meetings, several series of position papers were drafted
                    in the Department of State. Three papers were devoted to different aspects of
                    the question of treaty revision: WFM T–6d,
                    “Revision of the Italian Peace Treaty,” September 12, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra;</hi>
                    WFM T–6/1a, “Draft Documents Relating to the
                    Revision of the Italian Peace Treaty,” September 11, not printed; and WFM T–6/4, “Draft Declarations on the Italian Peace
                    Treaty,” August 10, not printed. These preparatory papers and their various
                    revisions are in CFM files, lot M–88, box
                    158.</p>
            </div>
